<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Banco Credito Provincial for sale.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Banco Credito Provincial for sale.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine private bank Banco Credito Provincial has been put up for sale after savers withdrew their deposits last week, local newspapers reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>According to business daily Cronista, four potential buyers have shown interest. They are Argentina's Banco Mercantil, Chile's Banco de Inversisn y Comercio, the U.S. New Bridge fund and an unnamed Italian bank.</p>
<p>Last week, shareholders in the bank increased its capital by 40 million pesos.</p>
<p>Banco Credito Provincial has 67 branches in Buenos Aires Province.</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668))</p>
